  "instance_name": "audience_id",
  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The target community for this meme is individuals who have experienced or can relate to interpersonal conflict within family dynamics, particularly involving ex-partners and their families. The meme appeals to people who may have had difficult or strained relationships with an ex-partner's family member, such as an ex-future mother-in-law, and who may use humor to cope with or express the emotional relief of no longer having to interact with such a person. The audience is likely to include adults navigating complex family relationships, especially those who have gone through breakups or divorces and are dealing with the emotional fallout involving in-laws. The meme also targets those who are familiar with or have observed the social stigma around using alcohol as a coping mechanism for stress or conflict, making the humor relatable to viewers who recognize this behavior as a common, albeit unhealthy, response to difficult social situations. The visual of the man drinking and the text 'when you don't have to see your ex future mother-in-law anymore' are designed to resonate with people who have faced similar emotional burdens and find humor in the idea of escaping such situations through intoxication.",
